# Rust
/target
/ros2/target
/target-wsl
**/*.rs.bk

# MuJoCo, downloaded by the build on first run (~19.5 MB)
/.mujoco

# Prebuilt tooling — Rerun viewer, portable Blender
/.tools

# Run output: recordings, logs, generated projections.
# The curated copies that belong in the repo live in media/ instead.
/out

# Generated assets. Regenerate with scripts/convert_glb.py — see assets/README.md.
# assets/demo/ is committed: it is the self-contained Quick Demo scene.
/assets/candi_obj
/assets/candi_mjcf
/assets/skydio_x2
/assets/candi_decimated.glb
/assets/candi.glb
/3dCandi

# Recordings and meshes are never committed: a source mesh alone is tens of MB
# and a single .rrd is 23-155 MB.
*.rrd
*.glb
*.obj
*.bt

# Secrets and local configuration. None of these are used by the project as it
# stands; they are listed so that adding one later cannot be committed by
# accident.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# Editors, OS and local tooling
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
/.claude/

# Cargo.lock is committed for both workspaces. This is an application: a
# reproducible build is the point, and the lockfile is what makes two people
# get the same dependency versions.
